      "publication_year": 2019,
      "publication_date": "2019-05-12",
      "abstract": "In this essay I discuss the ways that Marxism is read through the lens of Lacanian theory by Lacan\u2019s followers and not by Lacan himself. I distinguish between different Lacanian approaches to Marxism and between Lacan\u2019s diverse effects on the subjects that are approached. I scrutinize five affirmative effects, namely those of problematising, historicising, generalising, confirming and completing what is read. I first explicate these effects briefly in discussing classic works of the 1980s and then at length in presenting my own Lacanian approach to Marxism. I show how the realisation of such effects implies a Lacanization of Marxism and the resulting constitution of a Lacanian Marxism that I openly assume.",
